Description: Offline, private, instant voice dictation for Linux
 Quoth turns speech into text entirely on-device. Press a key, speak, and the
 transcription appears in the focused window. Your voice and text never leave
 the machine.
 .
 It runs whisper.cpp with a Vulkan GPU backend (AMD / NVIDIA / Intel) and CPU
 always, plus an optional Intel-NPU encoder offload via a bundled OpenVINO
 runtime and Intel's user-space NPU driver. The overlay uses a bundled
 gtk4-layer-shell for precise positioning on compositors that offer
 layer-shell, and elsewhere suppresses the pill and shows recording state via
 the system tray.
 .
 This package needs libadwaita 1.5 or newer (Ubuntu 24.04 or newer, Debian 13 or
 newer). On Ubuntu 22.04 or Debian 12, apt will refuse to install it; use the
 Flatpak instead, which bundles its own runtime.

